    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Walking through the fragrance hall of a department store can be an overwhelming experience. You are surrounded by mirrored counters, persistent sales associates offering paper blotters, and price tags that easily cross the £200 mark. It is easy to walk away feeling like luxury fragrance is an exclusive club with a steep entry fee.</p><p>The truth is that building a sophisticated perfume collection does not require spending thousands of pounds. What it requires is knowing what you are looking at: understanding fragrance families, recognising how scent interacts with skin chemistry, and knowing where your money actually goes.</p>"
      }
    },
