    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>The secret to shopping smart is separating the marketing mythology from the actual olfactory juice. When you understand the fundamentals of fragrance families and concentration levels, you stop paying for ornate bottle caps and start buying scents that perform exceptionally.</p><p>Here is how to navigate the world of luxury inspired perfumery, build a rotation for every season and setting, and stop making expensive mistakes at the checkout counter.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_614820f",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Understanding Fragrance Families: Fresh & Woody vs Warm & Amber",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Fresh and woody fragrances are the bedrock of versatile daytime wearing. Fresh profiles lead with bergamot, sea salt, green tea, and crisp citrus. They radiate with clean energy, project effortlessly in warm weather, and feel natural in the office and casual environments.</p><p>Woody anchors like cedarwood, vetiver, and sandalwood give these scents structural backbone, preventing them from evaporating into thin air and providing an understated, polished aura.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>Warm, amber, and gourmand fragrances operate on a completely different wavelength. Featuring rich vanilla, tonka bean, saffron, and resinous woods, these compositions rely on heavy molecular weight compounds that stay close to the skin.</p><p>They project with magnetic warmth, creating an intimate scent trail that feels irresistible during evening dinner dates, autumn gatherings, and chilly winter nights.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "section_padding": 60,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "heading": "<p>The science of inspired fragrance creation</p>",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_spacing": 25,
            "box_color": "#1C1917",
            "box_radius": 15,
            "box_padding": 45,
            "box_spacing": 35,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>A common misconception is that luxury perfumes cannot be accurately replicated. In modern perfumery, advanced gas chromatography and mass spectrometry allow master chemists to analyse the exact molecular structure of any fragrance formula down to the percentage point.</p><p>At Scentspired, our perfumers use these precise chemical blueprints to reconstruct the fragrance using the identical premium raw oils sourced directly from Grasse, France. The result is a scent profile that mirrors the original in nuance, depth, and performance.</p><p>Whether it is <strong>Timeless Grace</strong> (inspired by Coco Mademoiselle) or <strong>Addiction</strong> (inspired by Baccarat Rouge 540), you get the authentic olfactory journey from opening spray to 10-hour drydown.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#F5EFE6",
            "box_text_size": 17,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.9,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "subheading": "<p>How to test before you commit</p>",
            "subheading_size": 42,
            "subheading_color": "#1A1816",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Never judge a perfume solely from a paper strip or during the first sixty seconds after spraying. Paper blotters do not have body warmth, sebum, or skin moisture, which are essential for blooming the heart and base notes.</p><p>Always spray on clean skin—ideally the inside of your wrist or forearm—and give it at least twenty minutes. Take note of how the scent transitions from its opening burst into its true drydown signature.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 17,
            "bottom_text_color": "#2D2A26",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.9
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
